
- `apps/web/` — Next.js App Router app (port {{PORT_WEB}}, `http://{{HOST}}`), the BFF: the browser's only backend (BP §24; ESLint blocks `axios` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`). Server Components by default; every server-side `lib/` file starts with `import 'server-only'` (BP §3). Env goes through `lib/env.ts` (`requireEnv`, `requireSecret`, `appEnv()` — the server's own environment, never `NODE_ENV` in client code); logging through `lib/logger.ts`, the only console writer (ESLint enforces it); every state-changing route opens with `isAllowedOrigin` → rate limit → `readJson` from `lib/http.ts` (CP §6.1). The CSP is per-request with a nonce in `proxy.ts` (`lib/csp.ts`; external origins in `lib/csp-origins.ts`), which is why the root layout awaits `headers()` (CP §6.7); static headers live in `next.config.ts`. `output: 'standalone'`; `pnpm start` serves that build. Deploys to Vercel (one project, Root Directory = `apps/web`). Next vendors its docs at `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`; for Next APIs they beat training data. Pre-wired: react-hook-form + @hookform/resolvers, @vercel/analytics, @vercel/blob (client-upload only, BP §7 — never POST file bytes through a route handler), @ai-sdk/react, date-fns.
